{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You may not.</b> Scripture comes to establish a negative prohibition regarding this matter." "<b>You may not.</b> Rabbi Yehoshua ben Karchah says: Could it be you are able, but not permitted? — like its parallel, ״וְאֶת הַיְבוּסִי יוֹשְׁבֵי יְרוּשָׁלַיִם לֹא יָכְלוּ בְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל (יְהוּדָה) לְהוֹרִישָׁם״ (Joshua 15) — they were able, but not permitted, because Abraham had cut a covenant with them when he purchased from them the Cave of Machpelah. And they were not Jebusites, but Hittites — rather, after the name of the city, whose name is Jebus; so it is explicit in Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer (ch. 36). And so it is stated: ״כִּי אִם הֱסִירְךָ הָעִוְרִים וְהַפִּסְחִים״ (II Samuel 5) — these are statues upon which they had inscribed the oath." "<b>And the firstborn of your herd.</b> A warning to the priests." "<b>And the gift of your hand.</b> These are the first fruits (Sifrei; Makkot 17)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:48.847787713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}